Ladybird centers button content within its final flex-item height
even when that height can’t resolve descendant percentages.

Blink’s FlexLayoutAlgorithm::BuildSpaceForLayout() supplies a fixed
block size independently of SetIsInitialBlockSizeIndefinite(). Its
AlignBlockContent() centers within the final fragment block size,
clamping negative free space to zero for buttons.

Gecko’s nsFlexContainerFrame::ReflowFlexItem() supplies the final size
separately from mTreatBSizeAsIndefinite. The button’s content gets
safe centering through nsBlockFrame::EffectiveAlignContent(), and
nsBlockFrame::AlignContent() centers it using the final metrics.

WebKit’s RenderButton::updateAnonymousChildStyle() gives its inner
renderer automatic block-axis margins to center its content safely.
RenderFlexibleBox::canUseFlexItemForPercentageResolution() separately
decides if a flex item’s height can resolve descendant percentages.
